	(text "SNS-5 IMU placement: board center, stiffest area, axes aligned with the board\nedges and marked on silkscreen, continuous ground plane underneath.\nC20 / C21 100 nF at the Vdd_IO / Vdd pins.\nThe ESC silicone grommets are the vibration isolation (MEC-1)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 66.04 168.91 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "1f230a8d-5280-4a1f-b0b0-96c8673f80b6")
	)
	(text "SNS-4 baro placement: pressure port facing UP, no silkscreen and no conformal\ncoating on the port, room for an open-cell foam patch over it, away from the\nregulators (thermal gradient = drift) and away from the prop-wash board edges.\n\nSNS-3 rate ceiling from the datasheet (Rate x Time < 1 s):\n25 Hz allows 16x pressure oversampling, 50 Hz caps it at 8x.\nCSB tied to +3V3 (= VDDIO level) selects I2C. SDO to GND through R5 10k gives\naddress 0x76; a resistor rather than a short keeps SDO-as-interrupt available."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 160.02 133.35 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "3cbe97e2-6624-404a-9f86-72306b45aa1b")
	)
	(text "Barometer - SPA06-003 on I2C1, addr 0x76 (SNS-3)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 160.02 50.8 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "5e5b7927-c647-4aa5-beb8-1d8ca83c3bbe")
	)
	(text "SNS-1 SPI Mode 1: SDx and SCx tied to GND select the 4-wire SPI primary interface.\nOCS_Aux and SDO_Aux stay UNCONNECTED (soldered, no net) - they carry internal\npull-ups, so grounding them burns current and is out of spec.\nINT2 unused, no-connect flag.\nSPI1 clock 10 MHz max; F722 SPI1 prescaler /16 gives 6.75 MHz.\nFIRMWARE, first writes after reset: I2C_disable = 1 (CTRL4_C) and I3C_disable = 1.\nWith CS high the I2C/I3C slave is otherwise live on the SPI lines."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 66.04 138.43 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "9778a471-796d-4f49-83cd-0410189cff74")
	)
	(text "IMU - LSM6DSR on SPI1, dedicated CS (SNS-1)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 66.04 50.8 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "99142f75-ecab-4173-90d8-56c0dd6239c5")
	)
	(text "SNS-2 INT1 is an interface strap sampled at IMU power-up (high = I3C-only mode).\nNO pull-up on this net, EVER. R4 10k pull-down is the optional safe default;\nthe MCU pin stays input / low until the IMU is up.\nRouting INT1 to an EXTI-capable pin is mandatory, using it is optional\n(the loop may stay timer-paced)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 66.04 152.4 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "e4537c58-d8f2-42cc-95fe-4aa0fb690465")
	)
	(text "R6 / R7 4.7k are the ONLY I2C1 pull-ups on the board. They live on this sheet\nbecause the barometer is the primary I2C user; the GPS connector (CON-2) shares\nthe same bus and must NOT carry a second pair."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 160.02 158.75 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "fd527273-ada5-44ee-babe-fe698e775931")
	)
